[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) merged every report about a wrong date into one ticket and marked it
known, with one fix queued. Read against the tenant directory, the 412 reports hold **three
problems**. The queued fix covers only the first.

<Callout kind="warn">
Do not close #4471 when the parser fix ships. The booking form hint and the one-day moves are still open.
</Callout>

## The split

<ProblemSplit ticket={4471} />

- **`parser`** — the shared parser reads every date month first. Every tenant on file writes the
  day first, so their dates come out flipped (`7 April` becomes `4 July`). This is the bug #4471
  was written for, and it is most of the queue.
- **`hint`** — tenants on `booking-v3` (Alder Physio, Copper Studio, Pale Harbour) print
  `MM/DD/YYYY` under the date field. Their people type what the hint tells them, month first,
  and the form reads it the tenant's way. The reports look the same, but the parser fix does
  not touch them: the hint has to change. Only `form` reports qualify.
- **`oneDayMove`** — the month and the day number are right; the weekday is one day off. The
  desk read five reports this way ([desk notes](/kb/incidents/4471)): a Lisbon and a Toronto
  client got different days for one meeting, one invite arrived before the booking was made,
  and one tenant sees the move only in June. Nobody has found the cause yet. Treat it as
  unexplained until someone reproduces it. These five sit under `parser` in the older table
  below because they came from day-first tenants.

## Why the old count hid it

Intake tags a report from the reporter's browser, a guess. It disagrees with the cause the
tenant directory gives: of the `hint` reports, intake tagged 15 as `parser`, and it tagged 23
of the `parser` reports as `hint`. The tag cannot be used to merge. Decision
[0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject) merges on subject alone, and twelve subject lines
cover all 412 reports, so every cause shares them.

The ticket export also pages with overlap: it holds 427 rows for 412 reports. Count by id.

## The older view

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

## Next

- File and track the three problems separately, each with its count.
- Change the `booking-v3` hint to `DD/MM/YYYY` for day-first tenants, or make the form read what the hint says.
- Reproduce a one-day move before naming its cause.
- Replace decision 0001: merge on cause, not on subject. A decision is never edited, so this is a new record.

